ach of those hops fired exactly **once** over the whole horizon, so the chain has zero timing slack: it either happens to be ordered with gaps \u2264600 or it fails entirely \u2014 and no tool reveals those three timestamps or restricts to [5632, 44032].\n- Confounder control: 389 is the single most active node (625 events, step_10) with 281 in-neighbours (step_09). Its hub status makes a *static* path almost inevitable, so structural reachability here is weak evidence for a cascade \u2014 exactly the confound the task warns about. Likewise the 13 incident triangles (step_08) are time-agnostic.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_240c5b27\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [762, 1118, 389, 856, 1425],\n  \"window\": [5632, 44032],\n  \"confidence\": 0.7,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"762 never contacts 1118 directly and no 2-hop path exists: 762's out-neighbourhood {92,268,419,553,730,745,856,914,1269,1346,1368,1425,1466,1475,1513,1532,1643,1652,1705} is disjoint from 1118's in-neighbourhood. The only candidate routes are 3-hop chains through the hub 389 (762->856->389->1118, 762->1425->389->1118), and each constituent hop occurred exactly once in the entire horizon. Whether those three single events are increasing in time with consecutive gaps <